          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Start with the surface, not the brand. For a plain concrete driveway, buy a penetrating silane-siloxane sealer such as Foundation Armor SX5000, or Ghostshield Siloxa-Tek 8500 in a harsh, salty winter climate. For decorative concrete, a solvent-based acrylic like AR350 brings out the color, as long as you add grit and accept recoating every few years.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For asphalt, Latex-ite Airport Grade is the reliable middle choice, Black Jack Drive-Maxx 1000 gives the best finish on a smooth surface, and Henry keeps costs down on a driveway in good shape. Whichever surface you have, clean thoroughly, repair cracks first and seal in a dry, warm window, and the product will do its job.
